  "_scoringComment": "How long to wait for ai-service to score the anomalous transactions before giving up. Azure AI Foundry rate-limits scoring: every call takes an HTTP 429 and a ~3s retry before succeeding, so a full seed of ~23 transactions needs roughly 140s of scoring time. 90s could not finish and failed as though the consumer were dead.",
  "scoring": {
    "pollSeconds": 300,
    "pollIntervalSeconds": 5,
    "minScoredRequired": 1
  },
  "_approvalComment": [
    "Every approval below is proposed against a REAL subject discovered during seeding.",
    "`after` drives the post-propose transition that puts the approval in the demanded state:",
    "  leave-pending  -> stays pending; L1 so the banker sees it under NEEDS YOU",
    "  sign-slot0     -> requester signs slot 0 only; L2 so it sits in the supervisor's co-sign",
    "                    queue with one signature already collected (the co-signature story)",
    "  sign-full      -> signed to quorum",
    "  deny           -> denied by `denyBy`, terminalReason HUMAN_DENIED",
    "  supersede      -> a revised proposal replaces it; the original goes terminal with",
    "                    terminalReason PAYLOAD_SUPERSEDED (verification check 7.4)"
  ],
  "approvals": [
